§AA: the goblin gets a constitution, and the two-layer model gets scoped to data piles

Transcribes two rulings made 2026-09-21 and one tested mechanical fact. Nothing here designs — it
records decisions and a measurement, for the operator to strike through.

**The constitution requirement.** §AA made the rules machine-legible and never required them to be
legible to a person. Now it does: a goblin ships with a CONSTITUTION in shouty prose beside the hook
implementations, installing them is an honest visible step, and both sides read the same copy.
*"This is not like a background check."*

**Transitivity is the argument, and it is stronger than the offline one already in the doc.** A
constitution in the tree is the only form a party who was never in the original conversation can
check unaided — every alternative degrades on the second hop. §AA justified obeying-the-signs by
offline operation; this survives the original parties being gone, not just the network.

Also records the divestment move (sign the root, then remove your own key — self-authenticating,
becomes a mandatory ancestor, proves declaration and never destruction) as the same act one layer
down: removing the author from authority as publishing removes them from interpretation.

**Scoping the two-layer table**, which had been reading as the universal shape: it is the *data-pile*
case, where the point is being rewritable in a vacuum. A clone of the one branch that matters is
under no pressure to prove provenance at every hop, so a control branch can ship long before attested
execution is answered.

**One correction, measured.** "The shape of the idea" says a repository can be configured to behave
via hooks. `.git/hooks` is not in the object graph and survives neither a clone nor a bundle — tested
2026-09-21, along with submodule contents (`.gitmodules` travels, the contents do not). So the goblin
is tree-resident or it does not travel, `core.hooksPath` is the honest activation because the file you
read is the file that runs, and that activation belongs in the constitution rather than in an
assumption — station-node already paid for the alternative.

